course: dictionary
lesson: 2089
title: Contain: inside, made of, or under control
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Contain means to have something inside. «Each box contains 6 pencils» tells you that there are 6 pencils inside every box. To check a meaning, put it into the sentence: does a box that has 6 pencils inside contain 6 pencils? Yes, so it fits.
explain: Contain can also mean to be made of or to include something. «Food that contains nuts» has nuts as one of its parts. A food label that says «contains milk» is telling you that milk is in the food.
explain: Contain can mean to keep something under control, like containing a fire so it cannot spread. The words around it tell you which meaning is right. Read the whole sentence, then ask: what would fit here?
fact: Contain means to have something inside.
fact: Contain can also mean to be made of or to include something.
fact: «Dog poo can contain worm eggs» means worm eggs can be inside it, so it must be picked up and binned.
fact: «Mars looks red because its dust contains iron oxide» means iron oxide is one of the things in the dust.
fact: A container is something that holds things, like a box, bag or jar.
exercise: «Each box contains 6 pencils.» How many pencils are inside each box? | *6 | 60 | 3 | 16
exercise: «A box that contains toys» means what? | A box that is made of toys | A box that is painted red | *A box that has toys inside it | A box that someone has thrown away
exercise: «Water contains oxygen and hydrogen.» What does this tell you? | Water is cold and turns to ice | Water is a kind of gas that is always hot | *Oxygen and hydrogen are parts of water | Oxygen and hydrogen are sweet to taste
test: «Breathed-out air contains less oxygen and more carbon dioxide than breathed-in air.» What does contains mean here? | Has inside | *Has as parts, in amounts that can be compared | Is painted with | Keeps locked away
test: «The coins are gold-coloured, but they contain no gold.» What does contain no gold mean? | Have a gold box inside them | Keep gold locked away | *Are not made of any gold | Are gold but slightly brighter
exam: A food label says «contains milk». What does this tell you? | The food is white and cold | Milk is sold in another shop | *Milk is one of the things in the food |  | The food must be drunk quickly
